5. Field of Use Licensing Architecture
STALWART operates under a strict Field of Use (FOU) Licensing Framework. This model divides the software's deployment rights across distinct market segments, separating public-interest civic advocacy from high-stakes corporate and governmental compliance monitoring.

Tier 1: The Public Civic License (Zero-Cost / Open Access)
Authorized Users: Individual citizens, registered non-profits, local grassroots coalitions, municipal governments (populations under 100,000), and accredited investigative journalists.

Permitted Field of Use: Grassroots environmental auditing, local municipal zoning oversight, public-record translation, and community-level accountability campaigns (such as the Cosmo Superfund deployment).

Cost: Permanently free and open-source under standard community guidelines.

Tier 2: The Enterprise Commercial License (Monetized SaaS / API)
Authorized Users: Multinational corporations, real estate development portfolios, hedge funds, financial institutions, corporate law firms, and federal/state government compliance contractors.

Permitted Field of Use: Institutional regulatory tracking, predictive legislative risk assessment, multi-state corporate compliance monitoring, and automated portfolio impact modeling.

Cost: High-tier enterprise SaaS agreements, custom API integration fees, and multi-seat corporate licensing structures managed through Malt Studio.

Tier 3: The Restricted Defense & Pharma Intelligence Tier
Authorized Users: Regulated defense contractors, pharmaceutical enterprises, and federal agency oversight bodies.

Permitted Field of Use: Large-scale parsing of complex federal dockets (FDA, DoD, EPA) for corporate risk mitigation and automated Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) pipeline management.

Cost: Custom enterprise contracts incorporating mandatory audit logs and strict jurisdictional compliance boundaries.
